# lychee ignore patterns (regex, one per line)
# Use this to skip links that are flaky / not our responsibility to check.

# Publisher DOIs — these sometimes return 403 to bots but work for users
^https?://(dx\.)?doi\.org/
^https?://orcid\.org/

# OpenCollective — rate-limits bots with 403
^https?://opencollective\.com/

# GitHub edit-on-this-page links (only valid when logged in)
^https?://github\.com/[^/]+/[^/]+/edit/

# GitHub blob/file links — rate limited to 60/hr for unauthenticated
# requests. The links themselves are valid; CI just can't always verify.
^https?://github\.com/[^/]+/[^/]+/blob/
^https?://github\.com/[^/]+/[^/]+/tree/
^https?://github\.com/[^/]+/[^/]+/commit/
